Backstory

Bronnar was once the pride of the Geargrind clan, a promising artificer destined to bring his family renown. Unfortunately, “promising” turned into “volatile” when his mechanical auger-backhoe accidentally collapsed three mineshafts and singed the clan elder’s beard clean off. Banished from the halls, he now roams the surface world testing his “genius” inventions where the consequences won’t bury a whole city.

Despite the chaos, Bronnar’s heart is in the right place. He believes his inventions can make life better for common folk, even if they occasionally explode, catch fire, or attract lightning at inopportune times. Determined to win back his clan’s respect, he tinkers endlessly — with a hammer in one hand, a gear in the other, and a “totally safe” experimental prototype strapped to his back.

Stunts

Explosive Ingenuity: Once per session, declare you have exactly the gadget needed for the job (GM approval required). Gain +2 to Overcome rolls with Crafts when using said gadget.

Tinkerer’s Reflexes: Gain +2 to Crafts when creating an advantage in a physical conflict (e.g., traps, gadgets, distractions).

